"Test: $Slope con 2 variables en #equ
'<hr/>
'<h4>1. Funcion de 2 variables</h4>
g(x; y) = x^2 + 2*x*y + y^2
'<h4>2. Derivada parcial respecto a x (y fija = 3)</h4>
y = 3
S1 = $Slope{g(x; y) @ x = 1}
'<h4>3. Derivada parcial respecto a y (x fija = 1)</h4>
x = 1
S2 = $Slope{g(x; y) @ y = 3}
'<h4>4. Ambas derivadas en vector</h4>
x = 1
y = 3
V1 = [$Slope{g(x; y) @ x = 1}; $Slope{g(x; y) @ y = 3}]
'<h4>5. Funcion de 3 variables</h4>
h(x; y; z) = x*y + y*z + x*z
x = 1
y = 2
z = 3
S3 = $Slope{h(x; y; z) @ x = 1}
S4 = $Slope{h(x; y; z) @ y = 2}
S5 = $Slope{h(x; y; z) @ z = 3}
